  "body": "## What changed\n\nAdds an opt-in **Explain G-code** post option, with the engine side designed on #1358.\n\n- `PostOptions.explain` (default off). It is set per document or per setup through the existing undoable `SetPostOptions` / `SetSetupPostOptions` commands. `posting::options_value` publishes `postOptions.Explain = true` only when it is on. The project file writes an `explain` key (document and setup) only when it is on. With the option off, scripts and project files see exactly what they saw before.\n- New `crates/post/src/post/explain.rs`. It holds the `explain(words)` JS helper, loaded after the PRELUDE, plus the manifest reading (`explains = \"paren\" | \"semi\"`, optional `commentMax` 8..=255, default 60).\n  - The engine arms the helper only when the option is on. Unarmed, it returns `\"\"`, so Explain-off output is byte-identical.\n  - The helper strips `( ) ; %` and control characters, leads any active keyword with `- `, and cuts each comment to `commentMax`, cutting back to a whole meaning where it can.\n  - Unknown G/M words are skipped, not guessed.\n- With Explain on, a post whose manifest states no `explains` form (or an unknown one) is **refused by its name** before any hook runs. The refusal sits next to the #902 `programUnits` refusal (`units::post_name` is now shared).\n- `assets/posts/AGENTS.md` documents the manifest keys. The decision record is `docs/decisions/1386-explain-option.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` is green on 8c9705ee5: post suites, app suites (all goldens unchanged), and the ui operations/shell suites (14.8 min). Clippy `-p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings` is clean.\n- Pinning tests:\n  - `crates/post/tests/explain.rs`:\n    - `explain_on_comments_blocks_in_both_forms_and_strips_back_to_the_plain_program` (comments only; stripped output equals the Explain-off program)\n    - `a_post_without_explains_is_refused_by_name_before_any_hook`\n    - `explain_guards_the_comment_text_and_its_length`\n    - `explain_says_nothing_until_the_engine_arms_it`\n  - Unit tests in `explain.rs`: `the_option_reads_a_boolean_or_refuses`, `the_manifest_states_the_form_or_is_refused_by_name`.\n  - `crates/app/tests/explain_option.rs`:\n    - `explain_is_published_only_when_on`\n    - `the_explain_switch_undoes_redoes_and_round_trips_the_project_file`\n    - `a_setups_own_options_carry_explain`\n    - `every_builtin_explains_or_is_refused_by_name`\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No shipped post declares `explains` yet. The dialect opt-ins are #1387-#1389, so every built-in post refuses Explain-on for now, by name.\n- There is no dialog switch or MCP tool for the option yet (#1390).\n- The release/heavy lanes and pixel snapshots were not run.\n\nChangelog: Explain G-code post option - opt-in plain-English comments on G-code blocks for posts that declare a comment form; posts that do not are refused by name (#1386)\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #1386\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
